## SUB · Get price
Lesson Boss 4 (from 4.2). The get_price tool: input product (string), one product per call. Reads Price_List, matches by aliases (Boss 3 matching) and returns ONE small item:
- found: {"found": true, "name", "unit", "price", "stock"}
- not found: {"found": false, "suggestions": [...]}
- sheet down: {"error": "Price list unavailable, try again later"}

**Credential:** Google Sheets OAuth2.
**Replace:** YOUR_SHEET_ID.
Price_List columns: sku, name, unit, price, stock, aliases, active.

Test it alone (pin an input of {"product": "tomato"}): try tomato, big tatashe, pepper, yam.

parameters.jsCode:
// Input from the agent: one product, as the customer wrote it.
const trig = $('When Executed by Another Workflow').first().json;
const s = String(trig.product ?? trig.query ?? '').toLowerCase().trim();
const products = $('Price_List').all().map(i => i.json).filter(p => p.active !== 'no');

// Boss 3 matching: a product matches when one of its aliases appears in the words.
const hits = products.filter(p =>
  String(p.aliases).toLowerCase().split(',').map(a => a.trim()).some(a => a && s.includes(a)));

if (hits.length === 1) {
  const p = hits[0];
  return [{ json: { found: true, name: p.name, unit: p.unit, price: Number(p.price), stock: Number(p.stock) } }];
}

// Not found (or ambiguous): never return nothing. Suggest products that share a word.
// Words that mean more than one product (e.g. "pepper") are listed here on purpose.
const GROUPS = { pepper: ['Tatashe pepper', 'Rodo'] };
const words = s.split(/\s+/).filter(x => x.length >= 3);
let suggestions = hits.map(p => p.name);
for (const w of words) {
  if (GROUPS[w]) suggestions.push(...GROUPS[w]);
  for (const p of products) {
    if (String(p.name).toLowerCase().includes(w)) suggestions.push(p.name);
  }
}
suggestions = [...new Set(suggestions)].slice(0, 4);
return [{ json: { found: false, suggestions } }];
